  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two parallel wires <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Q\"></span> are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span>. Both wires carry the same current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span>, and the magnetic force per unit length between them is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The distance between the wires is tripled to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3d\"></span> and the current in both wires is doubled to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2I\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the new magnetic force per unit length between the wires after these changes?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2F}{3}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F}{3}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4F}{3}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{4F}{9}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
